# 🐛 bug report

I think this happens because a shared bundle with no entry is created in the case below (which in itself is correct).

```
AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: false == true
    at Object.apply (parcel/packages/runtimes/js/src/JSRuntime.js:182:9)
    at applyRuntimes (parcel/packages/core/core/src/applyRuntimes.js:54:44)
    at BundlerRunner.bundle (parcel/packages/core/core/src/BundlerRunner.js:112:5)
    at Parcel.build (parcel/packages/core/core/src/Parcel.js:268:25)
    at Parcel.run (parcel/packages/core/core/src/Parcel.js:156:18)
    at Command.run (parcel/packages/core/parcel/src/cli.js:244:7)
```

Check was added by https://github.com/parcel-bundler/parcel/pull/4033 (cc @wbinnssmith).

## 💻 Code Sample

```js
// index.js
new Worker("./main-worker");

// main-worker.js
import "./sync.js";
import("./async");

// async.js
import { minify } from "terser";
console.log(`transformer-${minify("").code}`);

// sync.js
import { minify } from "terser";
console.log(`utils-${minify("").code}`);
```


